Whenever clients do req to server over server container(TomCat)
They get sessionId created in the backend wrt successful login credentials first time.
Then throughout the session journey, same session Id is used to authenticate user
as HTTPServlets @RestControllers having HTTP(req/res)protocol are stateless and so needed to remind we are same user
k/a sessionId authentication by username password authentication filter in filterChain layer of Server,
for every other requests made until sessionId got expired etc..

RealLife ex-> use the credential for next login or stay signed in
 => in backend applications agree to use same sessionId like GMAIL, FaceBook Web etc..

 Issue comes CSRF(cross site request forgery) => any hacker/third party app or
 web introduced malicious scripts making request using ur current stolen sessionID to make request in your behalf to any server
 you are using to stole ur resource...

 =>CSRF taken care by SpringSecurity->except GetMapping, all other HTTP calls( are not allowed until you handle)

Ques> To handle the CSRF checks for POST,PUT,DELETE : we opt one of these ways:

1st>   we send same sessionId with all request but server send us a new CSRF_Token everytime
  which we pass in subsequent requests
OR,
2nd> we can send new sessionId on every req and disable CSRF from server
=> make http stateless or session stateless
OR,
3nd> use "sameSiteStrict" policy => no other site access it

 =================IMP===============
 So anytime we want to POST, PUT, DELETE we do require CSRF token if Spring-security is activated via dependency
 We pass X-CSRF-TOKEN in header from postman req

 while on browser Element code has _CSRF token while login and logout(http://localhost:8080/logout) inspection/devtool

 IMP:
 ====
 If we try to use browsers _CSRF or X-CSRF-TOKEN in postman(key : X-CSRF-TOKEN and value: browser-value)
 it will not work simply as they are two different clients for server...

 Solution: we can generate it from code/server(spring.security.web.csrf) using "HTTPServletRequest req" in parameter
 from  any method of type CsrfToken itself and return to client.
